Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(profiles): same-host cards name the real socket;
 release intent; no /tmp fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review round for the nopodman profile:

- The rulebook's GRANTED cards reused each catalog door's `use` text verbatim.
  Catalog text is written for a walled launch and cites in-box mounts
  (`/run/doors/<x>.sock`, or resolveDoor's `/run/<name>.sock` fallback) that do
  not exist same-host, so every card named a wrong path. `sameHostDoor` now
  appends `sameHostNote`: the real unix socket path and its `$<NAME>_SOCK`
  variable, declared authoritative. Tested for a catalogued and an
  uncatalogued door; doc paragraph updated.
- `runDir` refused to fall back to `/tmp` in its comment but did so in code
  when HOME was unset; it now throws (fail closed). Tested.
- `.release/nopodman-profile.md` (bump: minor): the patch adds two public
  entrypoints and the repo's mint convention wants an intent per user-facing PR.
- guest-room.test.ts removes the per-scenario run dirs it mkdtemps (afterAll),
  mirroring nopodman.test.ts; README claims pin for guest-room.test.ts
  regenerated (descriptor-kit `check .` → no drift).
- assertPrivateDir documents that it checks the immediate parent for
  other-writable only.

Refs: burndown gr-cowork-port (off-board; no tracking issue)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
